## Filing rules (Agentic OS)

These rules tell Claude where things go in this vault.

### Folders
- `raw/` — unprocessed inputs: notes, transcripts (`raw/transcripts/`), clippings, dumps. Drop anything here.
- `wiki/` — organized, durable knowledge. One idea or topic per note, linked with `[[wikilinks]]`.
- `outputs/` — finished deliverables:
  - `outputs/briefs/` morning briefs and daily plans
  - `outputs/research/` research briefs
  - `outputs/reviews/` weekly reviews

### When raw becomes wiki
Promote material from `raw/` to `wiki/` when it is something you'll want again: a concept you've
understood, a decision, a reference. Weekly reviews **suggest** promotions; nothing is moved
automatically. The raw source stays in `raw/` and the wiki note links back to it.

### Naming
- Date-prefixed, lowercase-kebab-case: `YYYY-MM-DD-short-title.md` (e.g. `2026-10-26-cell-membranes.md`).
- Evergreen wiki notes may drop the date: `spaced-repetition.md`.

### Safety
- Agents only ever **add** new files inside `raw/`, `wiki/` and `outputs/`.
- Never delete, move, rename or overwrite existing notes. To change something, write a new note and link it.
<!-- /agentic-os:filing-rules -->
